Acknowledged. There is no ask here for me to act on, so I am leaving
the port as posted; these items are for your poudriere build to settle.
Three things to watch for when you apply it.

The trailer lists six prerequisite-patch-id lines under base-commit
065036430e90. The diffstat touches only net-mgmt/uptrace and
net-mgmt/Makefile, but the patch was formatted on top of six local
commits that were never posted. If git am fails on that base, it is
most likely the net-mgmt/Makefile hunk, whose context depends on the
SUBDIR lines around it.

The port in "[freebsd-ports PATCH] net-mgmt/signoz: Observability
platform for logs, metrics, and traces" [1] also adds a SUBDIR line to
net-mgmt/Makefile, so whichever of the two lands second needs that
hunk refreshed.

The two ports differ in how they get the web UI. This one builds the
Vue frontend with USES=npm:pnpm; signoz uses upstream's prebuilt
assets. If the pnpm build gives poudriere trouble, the signoz approach
is a possible fallback, but only if upstream publishes a prebuilt
vue/dist for 2.0.3. I have not checked whether it does.

